Omission
- [N1] Node-level omission: i4:Once the Excel list is complete after a week, send it to the student. (reason: No element faithfully preserves the timing constraint; the corresponding action mutates it.)
- [N2] Node-level omission: i6:After typing the orders into the database, ensure that it is completed. Once the database is completed, control the incoming order. (reason: Database completion verification is entirely absent; replaced by a distorted control step.)
- [N3] Node-level omission: i9:If the order is worth less than 5.000 €, release it. (reason: Threshold logic is altered in the guard, leaving no faithful implementation of the '<' condition.)
- [N4] Node-level omission: i11:If the order is worth more than 5.000 €, send it for sign off and continue with the check. (reason: The 'continue with the check' branch is dropped, breaking the specified flow.)
- [N5] Node-level omission: i12:Contact the selling agency and upon receiving the actual issue, send the order for sign off. (reason: Complete absence of this intermediate routing and sign-off step in the model.)
- [N6] Node-level omission: i17:After PPC initiates production, the goods will be produced. (reason: The actual production step is never instantiated in the diagram.)
- [N7] Node-level omission: i21:Release the order via memo and ensure that the memo is achieved in the warehouse. (reason: Warehouse achievement verification is omitted from the flow.)
- [N8] Node-level omission: i22:Send the invoice and once it is sent, report the achievement to the finance department. (reason: Achievement reporting to finance is stripped, leaving only invoice dispatch.)
